        "content": "<!-- page 1: blocked by provider content filter; transcription unavailable -->\n\n---\n\nHere's a summary of the content on this page:\n\n## OIML Certificate of Conformity\n**Issuing authority:** NMi (OIML Member State: The Netherlands)\n\n**Certificate details:**\n- Number: R76/2006-NL1-17.22\n- Project number: 16200726\n- Page 2 of 2\n\n**Supporting Test Reports:**\n- No. NMi-16200726-01, dated 19 April 2017 (60 pages)\n- No. NMi-16200726-02, dated 19 April 2017 (33 pages)\n\n## Characteristics of the non-automatic weighing instrument\n\n| Characteristic | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Accuracy class | (III) |\n| Maximum capacity | 0 ≤ Max ≤ 15 kg |\n| Verification scale interval | e ≥ 2 g |\n| Weighing range(s) | Multiple range |\n| Max. number of scale intervals (multiple range) | n ≤ 3000 divisions (per weighing range) |\n| Maximum number of weighing ranges | 2 |\n| Tare | T ≤ Max₁ − e₁ for multiple range instruments |\n| Temperature range | −10 °C / +40 °C |\n| Power supply voltage | 100 – 240 V AC, 50/60 Hz |\n| Application | Intended to be used for direct sales to the public |\n| Software identification | Version number: 2.00 |\n\nThis page confirms conformity under OIML R76 (the international recommendation for non-automatic weighing instruments). The \"(III)\" class indicates a **medium accuracy commercial scale**, and the \"direct sales to the public\" designation means it's approved for retail use (e.g., selling goods by weight to customers).\n\nIs there anything specific about this certificate you'd like me to explain?"
